{"minimumTokenResponseSchema uses computed keys from z.string().toString(), producing a literal property name (e.g., 'ZodString') instead of validating arbitrary expiry fields; in sync mode this makes parsing fail and token refresh throw": 0.8723353743553162, "GoogleCalendarService writes the Zod safeParse result object ({success,data,...}) into Credential.key instead of the credential payload, so the next googleCredentialSchema.parse(credential.key) will throw and break the integration after the first refresh": 0.9765307307243347, "In sync mode, refreshOAuthTokens returns a Fetch Response, but several callers treat the return value as an SDK/axios object (accessing .data, .expiresIn, etc.), causing runtime exceptions during token refresh": 0.6835882663726807, "In zoho-bigin's CalendarService, refreshOAuthTokens() is called with credentialId (the credential row's database primary key) as the third argument, but the function parameter expects userId, causing the sync to target the wrong user or fail": 0.9870209097862244, "SalesforceCalendarService refreshes the OAuth token and updates the DB, but it creates the jsforce.Connection using the old credentialKey.access_token instead of the refreshed token, so API calls can still fail with an expired token": 0.9728571772575378, "The webhook handler does not restrict HTTP method and uses zod .parse(), symmetricDecrypt(), and JSON.parse() without error handling; invalid payloads or a misconfigured header name casing will return 500s instead of clean 4xx responses": 0.9667509198188782, "The webhook updates credentials via findFirst({ where: { userId, appId } }) even though Credential has no uniqueness constraint on (userId, appId), so users with multiple credentials for the same app can have the wrong record updated": 0.8435143232345581, "parseRefreshTokenResponse() throws an Error on parse failure, so it never returns a result with success: false. The .success checks in Salesforce and Zoom are unreachable dead code that misleads maintainers about the function's error-handling contract": 0.7789149880409241}